ragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙîWoe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸWoe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxThou blind Pharisee, cleanse first that which is within the cup and platter, that the outside of them may be clean also.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀWoe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men's bones, and of all uncleanness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfEven so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|and say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfWherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNYe serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÏWherefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: and some of them ye shall kill and crucify; and some of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and persecute them from city to city:¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁthat upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHVerily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book'§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse'¦verses“„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙáO Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ-Behold, your house is left unto you desolate.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyFor I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse'